# Auto detect text files and normalize end of lines to LF (\n)
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except Windows batch files, which must keep their CRLF line endings:
# cmd.exe fails a GOTO across a label in an LF-only file at runtime, with
# "The system cannot find the batch label specified". Marked -text rather
# than eol=crlf so the bytes are stored as-is; the existing .bat files are
# already committed with CRLF, and normalising them would rewrite every
# line of an otherwise untouched file.
*.cmd -text
*.bat -text
